{"task_id": "Mbpp/108", "solution": "def merge_sorted_list(list1: list, list2: list, list3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Merges three lists into a single sorted list, preserving duplicates and not mutating inputs.\"\"\"\n    # Concatenate all elements from the three input lists into a new list.\n    combined_list = list(list1) + list(list2) + list(list3)\n\n    # Sort the combined list in non-decreasing (ascending) order and return it.\n    return sorted(combined_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all given nested lists.\n    Assumes nested_lists contains at least one inner list, and elements are hashable.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common elements with the set of the first inner list.\n    # The problem implies nested_lists will not be empty.\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Intersect with subsequent inner lists.\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        common_elements.intersection_update(nested_lists[i])\n        # If common_elements becomes empty, no further intersection is needed.\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return common_elements"}
