{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def _left_cyclic_rotate(s: str, times: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Performs a left cyclic rotation on a string.\"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n    length = len(s)\n    effective_times = times % length\n    return s[effective_times:] + s[:effective_times]\ndef _generate_rotations(s: str, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Generates a list of k left-cyclic rotations of a string.\"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        return []\n    \n    rotations_list = []\n    current_rotation = s\n    \n    for _ in range(k):\n        rotations_list.append(current_rotation)\n        current_rotation = _left_cyclic_rotate(current_rotation, 1)\n        \n    return rotations_list\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times.\n    The original string is considered rotation 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Assuming valid binary_string and rotations as per problem constraints and \"no edge case checks\" instruction.\n    # _is_valid_binary is defined as per design but not explicitly called here,\n    # trusting the input to be non-empty and binary.\n\n    generated_rotations = _generate_rotations(binary_string, rotations)\n    \n    odd_count = 0\n    for rotated_str in generated_rotations:\n        # A binary number is odd if its least significant bit (rightmost character) is '1'.\n        # Since binary_string is assumed non-empty, rotated_str will also be non-empty for k > 0.\n        if rotated_str[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return odd_count"}
