{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates whether the given matrix is a magic square.\n    Validates input for square shape and integer elements, then checks sums of rows, columns, and diagonals.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list of lists.\")\n    \n    n = len(matrix)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix must not be empty.\")\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        if not isinstance(matrix[i], list):\n            raise ValueError(\"All rows in the matrix must be lists.\")\n        if len(matrix[i]) != n:\n            raise ValueError(\"Matrix must be square.\")\n            \n        for j in range(n):\n            if not isinstance(matrix[i][j], int):\n                raise ValueError(\"All matrix elements must be integers.\")\n\n    target_sum = sum(matrix[0])\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if sum(matrix[i]) != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    for j in range(n):\n        current_col_sum = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            current_col_sum += matrix[i][j]\n        if current_col_sum != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    primary_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        primary_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    if primary_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    secondary_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        secondary_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n    if secondary_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(input_list: list) -> object:\n    # Use a dictionary to store the frequency of each item in the input list.\n    counts = {}\n    for item in input_list:\n        counts[item] = counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    # Find the item with the maximum frequency.\n    max_freq = -1\n    max_item = None\n\n    # Iterate through the items and their frequencies.\n    # Dictionary iteration order (insertion order in CPython 3.7+) ensures deterministic tie-breaking\n    # by returning the first item encountered with the highest frequency.\n    for item, freq in counts.items():\n        if freq > max_freq:\n            max_freq = freq\n            max_item = item\n\n    return max_item"}
