{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if element x is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def find_first_occurrence(arr, target):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of target in arr using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    def find_last_occurrence(arr, target):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of target in arr using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    first = find_first_occurrence(array, x)\n\n    # If the element is not found, its count is 0, so it cannot be a majority.\n    if first == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last = find_last_occurrence(array, x)\n\n    count = last - first + 1\n    \n    return count > (n / 2)"}
