{"task_id": "Mbpp/281", "solution": "def all_unique(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in a list are unique, handling hashable and unhashable types.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    seen_hashable = set()\n    seen_unhashable = []\n\n    for item in input_list:\n        try:\n            # Try to hash the item. If successful, it's hashable.\n            # Check against the set of seen hashable items first.\n            if item in seen_hashable:\n                return False\n\n            # If not in the hashable set, check against previously seen unhashable items.\n            for u_item in seen_unhashable:\n                if item == u_item:\n                    return False\n\n            # If no duplicates found, add to the hashable set.\n            seen_hashable.add(item)\n\n        except TypeError:\n            # The item is unhashable.\n            # Check this unhashable item against ALL previously seen items (both hashable and unhashable).\n            for h_item in seen_hashable:\n                if item == h_item:\n                    return False\n            for u_item in seen_unhashable:\n                if item == u_item:\n                    return False\n\n            # If no duplicates found, add to the unhashable list.\n            seen_unhashable.append(item)\n\n    return True"}
