{"task_id": "Mbpp/414", "solution": "import collections.abc\ndef overlapping(seq1, seq2) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if any element from seq1 exists in seq2 (using ==), otherwise False.\n    Raises TypeError if seq1 or seq2 is not iterable.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(seq1, collections.abc.Iterable):\n        raise TypeError(\"seq1 must be iterable\")\n    if not isinstance(seq2, collections.abc.Iterable):\n        raise TypeError(\"seq2 must be iterable\")\n\n    # Convert seq2 to a set for efficient O(1) average time lookups.\n    set2 = set(seq2)\n\n    # Return False if either sequence is effectively empty.\n    # 'not seq1' handles empty lists/tuples/strings or exhausted iterators if converted to a list/tuple.\n    # 'not set2' handles cases where seq2 was empty.\n    if not seq1 or not set2:\n        return False\n\n    # Iterate through elements of seq1 and check for presence in set2.\n    for item in seq1:\n        if item in set2:\n            return True\n            \n    return False"}
