{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "def sum_digits(value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\n    Raises TypeError if value is not an integer, ValueError if negative.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_type(val) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the input value is an integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(val, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"value must be int\")\n\n    def _validate_non_negative(val: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the input integer is non-negative.\"\"\"\n        if val < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"value must be non-negative\")\n\n    def _split_digits(val: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Decomposes a non-negative integer into a list of its base-10 digits.\"\"\"\n        if val == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        while val > 0:\n            digits.append(val % 10)\n            val //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]  # Return digits in MSB-to-LSB order\n\n    def _compute_sum(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the sum of a list of digits.\"\"\"\n        return sum(digits)\n\n    _validate_type(value)\n    _validate_non_negative(value)\n    digits = _split_digits(value)\n    return _compute_sum(digits)"}
