{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locate the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\n    The input list is assumed to be sorted in non-decreasing order.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(list) # high is exclusive; the insertion index will be in [0, len(list)]\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        mid_val = list[mid]\n\n        # If mid_val is less than or equal to the value, the insertion point must be to the right of mid.\n        # This ensures the new value is placed to the right of any existing equal elements.\n        if mid_val <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            # If mid_val is greater than the value, the insertion point is at or to the left of mid.\n            high = mid\n\n    return low"}
